#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100647 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "a0f21b4c-0f5c-5567-aaec-9da481d2e7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-547" :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100648 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "0c84fc6d-422e-5729-94d2-a12cda71f78d" :question/math-academy-id "e-548" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100649 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "244bb10c-4c6f-5be0-bd9a-72b4defee245" :question/math-academy-id "e-549" :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "a1572338-79f7-5da7-b9f6-552dcb7984a6" :question/math-academy-id "e-550" :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a711b4cd-449a-5b67-bc2b-1daf47ab2a29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386151} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f4344c-5821-5448-bbf8-caf063e16d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386152} {:answer/id #uuid "8bc5d772-308a-5e43-9c75-bbf99a23b44c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386153} {:answer/id #uuid "f077af58-34cf-5d08-95a9-5150fb89c66b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386154} {:answer/id #uuid "78473b4c-b515-5fd8-8166-4e008255ff46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4f4344c-5821-5448-bbf8-caf063e16d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386152} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d01f545-648e-544e-bd81-bf3ed51943fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eef23b72-e36a-5c45-a5b3-e03a1d351b74" :question/math-academy-id "q-120298" :question/problem "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=6{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[-1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (2{x}^{3})|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(2)^{3}-2(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =6 \\\\ 6{c}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =1 \\\\ c & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d9bf282-58a1-5d82-b0e7-c72fdf9d90e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386158} {:answer/id #uuid "41901d4d-81c2-562f-abe2-33e08b75c0e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{16}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386159} {:answer/id #uuid "81d09b30-d0f9-5648-a9dd-72ef95d21227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386160} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a3cd76-835c-5485-b247-c563ad07c69f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386161} {:answer/id #uuid "2b3323d0-b849-5ade-bdce-8dad4c76f1da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d9bf282-58a1-5d82-b0e7-c72fdf9d90e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386158} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcd021c-11f6-5e32-90b2-c5143d5dbd98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2b64626-04c3-5fb9-a70b-3ec150e19575" :question/math-academy-id "q-120333" :question/problem "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=5\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}$ on the interval $[0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2{x}^{5/2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\cdot {2}^{5/2}-2\\cdot {0}^{5/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{{c}^{3}} & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e3208c6-746e-5199-90ad-789d0a4b2409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386165} {:answer/id #uuid "ef74a6b0-7f25-544b-b8ae-f7d47395dabf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2,\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386166} {:answer/id #uuid "b7cc8716-b4a7-5334-9599-1a521a91bffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386167} {:answer/id #uuid "e91cd08b-ba6d-527f-b8ad-1b84c3416576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386168} {:answer/id #uuid "88809e12-686d-52c1-966f-b7ab0228f703" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7cc8716-b4a7-5334-9599-1a521a91bffa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386167} :answer-field/id #uuid "61d61f9f-b9eb-5c9d-8c61-aefcbb45c2a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "645765fa-26ae-5ed8-a0d8-99efa4f8225a" :question/math-academy-id "q-120450" :question/problem "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-9{x}^{2}+14x-2$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-9{x}^{2}+14x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-3{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-3{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-2c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-3{c}^{2}+7c-2 \\\\ 3{c}^{2}-7c+2 & =0 \\\\ (c-2)(3c-1) & =0 \\\\ c & =2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} {:answer/id #uuid "93a81b6f-340c-5a38-93ca-46a5ff16f29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342311} {:answer/id #uuid "2383bcff-b9da-593f-88c2-e89a2f61299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342312} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca59082-0a28-52be-80e6-2e8a54550b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342313} {:answer/id #uuid "8a29d6a2-873c-5695-b181-655cccae2a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} :answer-field/id #uuid "40a81efe-bb81-5712-8a60-556d0e16bd14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ba1202f-23bb-59b7-8a58-51ad745d9aba" :question/math-academy-id "q-15225" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "404e9f9c-aace-5a13-85bf-68c2cfbc6896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386172} {:answer/id #uuid "ea863b2c-2f4f-59f2-aa56-01a4f179ef4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386173} {:answer/id #uuid "bc641657-f01d-5448-868b-b2f2e9979abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386174} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4f1599-3de3-5096-9d83-500f1b467fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386175} {:answer/id #uuid "e564d2b2-f995-5714-b7c9-a3a83e4f5605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb4f1599-3de3-5096-9d83-500f1b467fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386175} :answer-field/id #uuid "c99991c4-91d3-56e9-86a4-3e7f15632f3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fbfdded4-c230-5698-b4cd-d1a52f9642db" :question/math-academy-id "q-18143" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/7eddb6203ccc3eead9a2a89d7868d3206af52be4c269962e33c551ddd3cf08cd.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-4,4],$ is shown above. It consists of six line segments.  Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-1,3].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-(-1)}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de014ad-2055-5349-9244-64ad84e18e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386179} {:answer/id #uuid "e3abe82d-e288-51a6-a112-e9d1b2bc0aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386180} {:answer/id #uuid "a85a5c86-d002-5709-9803-6467b782f27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386181} {:answer/id #uuid "1413b167-c304-5d75-a8ed-cab2474cc2f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386182} {:answer/id #uuid "d9799a52-0244-5aec-b5ca-0ebcd18def1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9799a52-0244-5aec-b5ca-0ebcd18def1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386183} :answer-field/id #uuid "5212c4b8-99cc-5faa-87db-05ad7d8c8963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4b62ed1-12e5-5a6e-aad0-bc0c6b0adfd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-2474" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=-x+2$ on the interval $[-2,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals. we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(-x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2x)|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+2\\cdot 2)-(-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}+2\\cdot (-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[2-(-6)] \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ -c+2 & =2 \\\\ c & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7561c120-2dd2-5147-a914-b9d8055b13e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386186} {:answer/id #uuid "87172de7-e0a9-5165-8750-ad28138c18b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386187} {:answer/id #uuid "0c224cc2-de66-57d2-b97a-b6ee32f04489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386188} {:answer/id #uuid "2b4da1d6-8785-5852-983c-273d5447277e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386189} {:answer/id #uuid "d89224a4-7338-5554-b49a-7e20f0f12bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87172de7-e0a9-5165-8750-ad28138c18b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386187} :answer-field/id #uuid "dce538c8-a1b8-5237-b33b-7e091e8514e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "861d7909-aecf-5978-9bba-b5634c19846a" :question/math-academy-id "q-2476" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=4+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ on the interval $[1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(4+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(4x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}})-(4\\cdot 1-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{4}-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =\\frac{19}{4} \\\\ 4+\\frac{2}{{c}^{3}} & =\\frac{19}{4} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{c}^{3}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{c}^{3}}{2} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ {c}^{3} & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{8}{3}} \\\\ c & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a9cb877-f670-5acc-be10-454cec272525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099212} {:answer/id #uuid "e8090f80-705e-5379-9f3d-5e9d20ce0098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099213} {:answer/id #uuid "fc399a7d-96fe-5e54-9af7-f48f16fa8fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099214} {:answer/id #uuid "65106760-2d63-5dd2-a3d5-5e0e8d3d1de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099215} {:answer/id #uuid "781b84f8-7658-5344-b5c8-a8ee9e808812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8090f80-705e-5379-9f3d-5e9d20ce0098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099213} :answer-field/id #uuid "64ca97ca-0196-5ed0-8abe-82f6d68edd1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28111792-cb9a-53d6-8e29-9d2f2d29b33c" :question/math-academy-id "q-2491" :question/problem "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=3{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[-2,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ({x}^{3})|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{2}^{3}-(-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4 \\\\ 3{c}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2285b351-3144-5af3-8c46-2b7da81a7ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386193} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7de4e6-1c18-5e63-954f-1af030a0a984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386194} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5891c3-61a1-5005-9fa6-f33121a7766d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386195} {:answer/id #uuid "5486a4db-79dd-5af5-92ca-4cf84540f79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386196} {:answer/id #uuid "0475e6ab-edab-5c23-bf18-ca5014dabcec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0475e6ab-edab-5c23-bf18-ca5014dabcec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386197} :answer-field/id #uuid "65f4a48a-0645-5349-9e19-34bf740f062b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21ad90ae-5ee1-51ed-8041-81806b6326c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-30771" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-2x$ on the interval $[-2,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-{x}^{2})|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {1}^{4}-{1}^{2})-(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-(-2)^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{3}{4}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "672e9ba0-e2be-5a8f-a78a-6bb819f35c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291195} {:answer/id #uuid "f49fc375-5782-572e-8f2c-7a9cf21ca337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291196} {:answer/id #uuid "9695b549-f9eb-58e7-b607-8000ed32121d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291197} {:answer/id #uuid "b99675fb-9a01-5b54-8ba3-4589872f6cd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291198} {:answer/id #uuid "6871dfb7-e709-540e-bc17-835ef63ad935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9695b549-f9eb-58e7-b607-8000ed32121d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291197} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ae9fb8-6a3d-58fa-892f-b68188b64c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41a9e5db-75da-5502-afac-88828e98449b" :question/math-academy-id "q-30776" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $g(x)=2{x}^{3}-x-1$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{0-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x)|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(8-2+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb1679d-d1ea-53fa-b29c-8f05e0a0593e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386200} {:answer/id #uuid "a35beb41-be5d-5150-83f9-b2566774d060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386201} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9da9e5-c033-59c1-97b0-536672acbf2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386202} {:answer/id #uuid "628e2732-9e24-5921-b8fa-629cbe975ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386203} {:answer/id #uuid "848814d5-c847-56f3-82e7-1969063db4ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cb1679d-d1ea-53fa-b29c-8f05e0a0593e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386200} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b132c79-ba4e-5ead-9b93-15a76ca38b7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8da72f4-4be3-59c9-b893-26555f51f2de" :question/math-academy-id "q-30893" :question/problem "Within the interval $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ determine the average value of $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(0+(-1))-(0+1)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afabe4d8-7a6f-581e-ac7c-40d1a4a33283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "230-\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386207} {:answer/id #uuid "588dc3dd-bc80-5888-bda7-d183057799e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "220+\\frac{5}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386208} {:answer/id #uuid "b48ce326-1c17-5a52-838e-b1887171d52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200+\\frac{16}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386209} {:answer/id #uuid "b09a779d-8273-58dd-857f-a62049401af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200-\\frac{12}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386210} {:answer/id #uuid "86ac5ef3-a422-5fb8-a11c-5d3923356efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210-\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48ce326-1c17-5a52-838e-b1887171d52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200+\\frac{16}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386209} :answer-field/id #uuid "a391066b-1032-502e-9574-3f5785d5542e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4c918188-0e18-5c96-8d7f-113270e439f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-30903" :question/problem "A biologist found that the population $P$ of some bacteria in a petri dish can be modeled by the function $P(t)=200+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}t),$ where $t$ is the number of hours after $12$ noon. Find the average number of bacteria during the period from $12$ noon to $4$ p.m." :question/worked-solution "Since the function is valid starting from $12$ P.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,4].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}P(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-0}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(200+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}t))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}(200t-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\,t}{4}))|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(200\\cdot 4-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 4}{4}))-(200\\cdot 0-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{4}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(800-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(800-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))+\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\cdot 1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[800+\\frac{32}{\\pi }+\\frac{32}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(800+\\frac{64}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =200+\\frac{16}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb1a3ab-a4c6-55b8-8739-6a5c9cda8e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0eb1a3ab-a4c6-55b8-8739-6a5c9cda8e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386214} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9bf128c-1b88-5b9e-adb7-7ee48e4e7610" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c37489-1167-5f71-92ca-47c1b702b12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30c37489-1167-5f71-92ca-47c1b702b12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386216} :answer-field/id #uuid "e75cd6b8-f7c8-52e8-91d7-6dc307047c9c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89716bdf-323f-525b-8018-ace34761dc72" :question/math-academy-id "q-316306" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the **exact** nonzero values of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=12{x}^{2}-16x-12$ over the interval with endpoints $0$ and $c$ is equal to $0$ are\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and  $\\,c=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c\\ne 0,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(12{x}^{2}-16x-12)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}-12x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(4{c}^{3}-8{c}^{2}-12c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =4{c}^{2}-8c-12 \\\\ 0 & =4({c}^{2}-2c-3) \\\\ 0 & =4(c-3)(c+1) \\\\ c & =-1,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in **ascending order**, the values of $c$ are \n\n$$\nc=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,c=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53eb00fe-4f55-552c-8c93-84099ec474f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53eb00fe-4f55-552c-8c93-84099ec474f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291205} :answer-field/id #uuid "60610310-2ac4-5ae9-a341-f1deb1d8f329" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e56f391c-b858-5626-9202-9c04093762c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-316307" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-20+80-10=50.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-8)}\\cdot (50) \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c039ea78-e776-5206-8e89-f17e9e3aa758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291229} {:answer/id #uuid "9debab67-805d-5409-b59d-638c831040c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9debab67-805d-5409-b59d-638c831040c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291230} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b1da21-91a7-5b46-85c0-256a1c75b6d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bfc3ffe0-eb79-55a0-9876-0723bc5ad393" :question/math-academy-id "q-344596" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-8x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(6{x}^{2}-8x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{3}-4{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ -12 & =2{c}^{2}-4c-10 \\\\ 0 & =2{c}^{2}-4c+2 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-2c+1 \\\\ 0 & =(c-1)^{2} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b54b43-3c84-5656-be36-ea9c956fb491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27b54b43-3c84-5656-be36-ea9c956fb491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291240} :answer-field/id #uuid "43776673-5b88-5afd-9826-30b5c8f2c3f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "752704cb-a8ad-55ac-ac26-51b58834ab35" :question/math-academy-id "q-344648" :question/problem "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{7}}{7})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }[(-1)^{7}-{1}^{7}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cdfcd64-e975-5f9a-a87e-656249c63b24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f43cc69-bbf5-5e06-8e03-26d2b66ad73a" :question/math-academy-id "q-344702" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b70ac59-eb21-505d-a7dc-f2de47828d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386219} {:answer/id #uuid "2d57212b-05d0-52e6-a8fc-c40c4fb34078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386220} {:answer/id #uuid "a492f9f4-9c9d-5c8f-a371-ab13ec4ada8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386221} {:answer/id #uuid "d3144dae-8030-59f4-813f-2ca1a571ac05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386222} {:answer/id #uuid "c3aabe9a-f5f7-56e7-b317-98ccfa5b920c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b70ac59-eb21-505d-a7dc-f2de47828d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386219} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bf47106-1eaf-5ef4-9d82-8027465c0a9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aaa57727-9ab3-5495-b558-e512a24ae7a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74069" :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-3\\sqrt{x}$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-6.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-3\\sqrt{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -6 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3/2})|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -6 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3/2})-(0)] \\\\ -6 & =-2\\sqrt{c} \\\\ \\sqrt{c} & =3 \\\\ c & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9874b151-c44a-57b4-bf45-da4fd9dae072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386226} {:answer/id #uuid "c254bb8a-73d2-58cd-becf-150c62302006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386227} {:answer/id #uuid "8090e378-a201-589b-a78f-24fe960a065c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386228} {:answer/id #uuid "6b1c9533-4931-5bcf-8479-f763ed10be3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386229} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6f7dde-de31-535f-b919-ce47ddd008e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9874b151-c44a-57b4-bf45-da4fd9dae072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386226} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4094d65-6b28-5a5e-a444-6c61b553b938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c33b9e25-c244-5fd5-9945-ea60f2a3eb1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-74072" :question/problem "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-24x+23$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3{x}^{2}-24x+23)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}({x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+23x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[({c}^{3}-12{c}^{2}+23c)-0] \\\\ -12 & ={c}^{2}-12c+23 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-12c+35 \\\\ 0 & =(c-5)(c-7) \\\\ c & =5,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aadbaaa8-2eb9-5504-804e-2a8da4ed0196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386233} {:answer/id #uuid "7e914cbe-1fe9-5d44-9e8d-81ff0cc9804d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{8}-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386234} {:answer/id #uuid "0a5d8f94-1493-5952-9ba9-eabf150eaf51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{8}+\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386235} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd55be5-ac16-5930-b91f-c064a56cf8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386236} {:answer/id #uuid "781f9926-f7c3-5368-9ed7-dcc69b8b25b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cd55be5-ac16-5930-b91f-c064a56cf8ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386236} :answer-field/id #uuid "391e9439-8564-54f1-a7f8-c3e4de1a8ec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa6fc6e8-f5ff-590f-accd-6b5cf81b87bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-74172" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/7ecbb53bb87156d11f9a9d8021182cdfb8c0c1749cd028780377bb61f32adf43.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-3,6]$, is shown above. It consists of the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(0,0)$ with radius $3,$ and two line segments. Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,5].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,3].$ The corresponding region is a semi-cirle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-(-3)}\\cdot (\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{16}+\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
